A||||2||btoth||Seat alignment||||5||
Z||000000||btoth||12-29-2001||11:39 AM||||How can I make sure that the seat track is properly aligned after removing and reinstalling?<P>There are currently a couple positions that don't properly lock into place like they should.||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||12-29-2001||02:12 PM||||There is only one way it will mount to the frame of the car (four 13mm nuts) and only one way the tracks can mount to the seat (four 13 mm bolts) - the problem, more than likely is a weak detent spring which is not allowing full engagement of the latch mechanism.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-29-2001||03:29 PM||||Take the seak back out and make sure the latch(s) and the locking holes aren't boogered up. One or more holes may have a burr in it. make sure everything is lubed. use a light grease in the rails.<P>as long as rails are locked durring install... they are pretty much self aligning.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
